Built into the file by `node build.js --vendor`
----------------------------------------------

three.js and jsPDF are embedded in the output. Both are MIT, which requires the
copyright notice to be included with the distribution; both minified builds
carry their own `@license` header and those headers are embedded verbatim, so
the notices travel with the artifact. `npm run test:offline` asserts they are
still present.

The OpenCascade reader is never embedded — it is 6 MB and only a STEP import
needs it — so STEP support remains network-dependent in every build.

